Sigil fixes to riscv-dv's Python generator (pygen) at riscv-dv
0d71c2b666dec48dde0b804a2138426da56aa252, applied by
scripts/riscv_dv_setup.sh to a copy in build/riscv-dv/gen (the clone in
third_party/riscv-dv is never modified; the copy's .py files are
converted to LF line endings first). Issue #8, docs/VERIFICATION.md.
Most hunks carry a "Sigil patch" comment. What each fix is for:

A  isa/riscv_instr.py: `from imp import reload` -> importlib (Python
   3.12 removed imp).
B  riscv_asm_program_gen.py: without sub-programs the main program gets
   the whole +instr_cnt (SV: main + sum(sub) == instr_cnt; pygen drew
   the main count from [10, instr_cnt]).
C  riscv_asm_program_gen.py setup_misa: a target with a read-only misa
   sets MISA_VALUE in its core setting; write exactly that value, so a
   writable-misa ISS (Spike) keeps the same extensions.
D  isa/riscv_b_instr.py: ratified spellings for draft-0.92 B mnemonics
   whose encodings were ratified under new names (pcnt -> cpop,
   sbset/sbclr/sbinv/sbext[i] -> bset/bclr/binv/bext[i]).
E  isa/riscv_instr.py build_basic_instruction_list: EBREAK/C.EBREAK/
   DRET/WFI were added as strings (KeyError: 'EBREAK' with
   +no_ebreak=0) and SYNCH as a nested list.
F  riscv_privileged_common_seq.py: rcs.implemeted_csr typo.
G  riscv_amo_instr_lib.py: avail_regs re-declared in the AMO base
   stream (pyvsc AttributeError on construction).
H  randrange(0, n - 1) -> randrange(0, n) and randrange(0, 1) ->
   randrange(0, 2) everywhere: SV $urandom_range is inclusive, so the
   last list entry was never picked and a one-entry list raised.
I  riscv_instr_stream.py randomize_instr: re-pick (up to 32 times) when
   the picked instruction cannot meet the stream's register
   constraints (e.g. a compressed op vs avail_regs) instead of failing.
J  riscv_amo_instr_lib.py: reserve the elements of rs1_reg (a list).
K  test/riscv_instr_base_test.py: recursion limit 20000 (deepcopy of
   the AMO stream objects).
L  riscv_amo_instr_lib.py: LR/SC/AMO address registers as in SV: rs1 is
   the stream's base register, rd must differ from it (pygen left LR/SC
   rs1 free and forced the AMO rd into the base registers).
M  isa/riscv_instr.py get_rand_instr: SV semantics (candidates =
   supported instructions narrowed by include_instr and by the
   included categories/groups, minus the excluded). pygen looked
   categories up by enum where the tables are keyed by name (the AMO
   stream drew from every instruction) and ignored exclusions whenever
   an include list was given.
N  test/riscv_instr_base_test.py: with one test per process run it
   in-process; a sys.exit() in a multiprocessing worker hung the pool.
O  riscv_loop_instr.py: loop counter/limit init and counter update are
   ADDIs with the constrained values, the backward branch compares the
   counter with the limit register, and loops nest as in SV (pygen used
   unconstrained random instructions, so loops need not terminate).
P  riscv_instr_stream.py mix_instr_stream: positions from [0, cnt-1] as
   in SV; [0, cnt] let the last instruction of a contained stream land
   before earlier ones (a loop branch ahead of its counter update).
Q  isa/riscv_b_instr.py is_supported: operator precedence made every B
   group except Zbb ignore +enable_b_extension.
R  riscv_amo_instr_lib.py: LR and SC of the same width. A mismatched pair
   (e.g. lr.w + sc.d) has an implementation-defined SC outcome (the
   reservation set must contain the SC's bytes: Sigil reserves exactly
   the LR's bytes, Spike accepts any SC to the LR address).
S  riscv_load_store_instr_lib.py: load/store streams as in SV: address =
   base + offset exactly, inside the data page, offset within the
   locality range (pygen used base+offset-1 or base+offset and never
   range-checked); the allowed instruction list starts afresh for each
   access (pygen kept extending one list, so c.lwsp etc. allowed for a
   small offset stayed allowed for offsets the encoding cannot hold:
   assembler "illegal operands"); the base register is never x0 or a
   reserved register (rs1_c was commented out: "la zero, ..."), and the
   SP-reserved check tests membership in either list. The hazard
   stream's own randomize_offset gets the same address fix (its
   misaligned ld/sd ended tests early in the generic exception handler)
   and draws the reuse-previous-address decision per access, as in SV.
T  riscv_privil_reg.py, riscv_privileged_common_seq.py: SSTATUS and SIE
   field layouts (from SV, plus VS), and no riscv_reg.randomize() for
   SSTATUS (broken in pygen; the MSTATUS path never calls it): S-mode
   boots aborted with "reg SSTATUS is not supported yet".
U  riscv_asm_program_gen.py gen_privileged_mode_switch_routine: the
   mode-switch code was collected in a list that the next loop
   iteration reset, so only M-mode boots got their mstatus setup and
   mret; +boot_mode=s/u programs silently stayed in M-mode.
V  riscv_instr_gen_config.py: without +boot_mode, boot in a random
   supported mode (SV boot_privileged_mode_dist_c; a TODO in pygen, so
   every program booted in M-mode). Chosen after seeding.
W  riscv_asm_program_gen.py gen_trap_handlers: the S-mode trap handler
   section for S/U boots, as in SV (stvec points at it; link error
   "undefined reference to stvec_handler" otherwise). pygen does not
   delegate traps (gen_delegation_instr is a TODO), so traps still go
   to M-mode.
X  isa/riscv_instr.py get_load_store_instr/get_instr: deep copies of
   the instruction templates (SV clone()). Shallow copies shared the
   operand fields, so all loads/stores of one kind printed the operands
   randomized last (a load using another stream's base register,
   reading an unmapped address).
Y  riscv_directed_instr_lib.py riscv_jal_instr: exclude the reserved
   registers from the jal rd one by one (not_inside(<vsc list>) did
   nothing; "jal tp" clobbered the trap handlers' stack pointer).
Z  riscv_loop_instr.py: loop counter and limit registers all distinct
   (SV unique {cnt, limit}); "bge t3, t3, target" looped forever.
AA isa/riscv_compressed_instr.py: compressed FP loads/stores (c.fld,
   c.fsd, c.fldsp, c.fsdsp, c.flw family) print FP register operands
   and "(sp)" (integer register names: assembler "illegal operands").
AB riscv_load_store_instr_lib.py gen_load_store_instr: the "unaligned"
   branch was indented under the 8-byte alignment test instead of under
   `if not cfg.enable_unaligned_load_store`, so every access that was
   not 8-byte aligned allowed lh/sh/lw/sw/ld/sd: programs hit misaligned
   traps, which end a riscv-dv test in the generic exception handler.
AC riscv_asm_program_gen.py: exception dispatch as in SV (ECALL from U
   and S as well as M, and BREAKPOINT) and an ebreak handler (a TODO in
   pygen) that resumes after the 2- or 4-byte ebreak; the first ebreak
   used to end riscv_ebreak_test.
AD riscv_instr_gen_config.py ra_c: the return-address register differs
   from the configured sp/tp registers (pygen compared with the literal
   x2/x4, so "jal t6" could overwrite the kernel stack pointer t6 and the
   next trap handler trapped forever).
AE riscv_asm_program_gen.py: a misaligned load or store/AMO exception
   resumes after the 2- or 4-byte access (misaligned_handler, like the
   ebreak handler) instead of ending the test in test_done. Sigil traps
   every misaligned access, so riscv_unaligned_load_store_test ended at
   its first one (about 240 records and one trap per run).

